Yes. So duplicate key path compensates twice. Also note in deadlock retry, after retry succeeds no issue. Severity: in REDIS_PREALLOC mode, Redis available inflated by qty; since Redis prealloc only gates early (DB is source of truth and will reject if DB insufficient), the risk is Redis allowing an order that DB then rejects → 409, not oversell. But it also means `sync`/align corrects within 30s. So it's not data corruption in DB; it's a consistency bug — major? I'd call it major (Redis counter drift → spurious stock availability, could cause user-visible false availability then 409). Actually if Redis is inflated, an order gets preallocated in
